invariant: INV-16
file: p256_field.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh p256_field
reason: returning the borrow as a bit rather than as a whole mask leaves
  every select keeping bit 0 of one side and the other 31 bits of the
  other. p256_field_harness.c states sub_limbs's contract as a mask and
  fails on this for any limbs at all, where a vector fails only for the
  operands it carries. Each run is a proof, so this belongs to the
  nightly's test-invariants-proof-backed job, never the fast tier.

--- old
    return (uint32_t)(diff >> 32);
--- new
    return (uint32_t)((diff >> 32) & 1u);
